  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Vocal Observer/Controller Environment (VO/CE)",
    "description": "Voice Observer/Controller Environment (VO/CE) is a system which integrates a COTS speech recognition product with the CTC OIS eGreenBook thus enabling hands-free operation of select applications developed by Lockheed Martin Combat Training Center Objective Instrumentation System (CTC OIS).  CTC OIS is incorporating technologies which provide Observer/Controllers (O/C) with custom applications to form an electronic version of their current Greenbook.  These applications streamline and improve the reporting process.  The CTC OIS tools support the ability to prepare a plan for training events, record observations, and generate reports which are later compiled into an After Action Review.  \n\nUsability feedback studies conducted by CTC OIS with the customer have determined that O/Cs would benefit from a speech recognition system which will support vocal user interface commands verified through visual cues on the display screen.  The VO/CE will allow the O/C to open reports, enter data, and send them through a hands-free interface. This system will minimize the difficulties related to typing and using a stylus in the training environment while O/Cs are occupied with tasks like driving, hiking, or wearing cumbersome clothing. ",
